According to the Hong Kong Public Libraries, the selection criteria for purchasing general library materials include:

- Whether the item is contrary to the interests of national security;
- Conformity with the direction of collection development;
- Subject coverage;
- Timeliness and accuracy;
- Authoritativeness and reputation of the author(s) and/or publisher;
- Style and clarity of presentation;
- Format;
- Demand;
- Price; and
- Literary merits (for fiction).

These criteria are used by professionally trained staff to assess the suitability of materials for acquisition, with recommendations made by branch librarians and endorsed by the Collection Development Meeting.
